📚 Scenario: Configuring Docker CRI with cri-dockerd

Context
Since Kubernetes removed the internal "dockershim," you must use an external CRI adapter like cri-dockerd to use Docker as your container runtime.  

Requirements
1. Install CRI Adapter: Install the cri-dockerd Debian package.  
2. Service Management: Enable and start both the cri-docker.service and cri-docker.socket.  
3. Kernel Configuration: Configure sysctl parameters for networking and connection tracking.  

🛠️ Solution Strategy
Step 1: Install & Start Services
Use the local cri-dockerd .deb package provided in the exam environment.  
Example: sudo dpkg -i cri-dockerd_*.deb

Reload systemd:
 systemctl daemon-reload

Enable and start the socket and service:
 systemctl enable --now cri-docker.socket cri-docker.service

Step 2: Configure System Parameters (sysctl)
Load required kernel modules first:
 sudo modprobe br_netfilter
 sudo modprobe overlay

Create a configuration file at /etc/sysctl.d/k8s.conf with the following parameters:  
    net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables = 1   
    net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables = 1   
    net.ipv4.ip_forward = 1   
    net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding = 1   
    net.netfilter.nf_conntrack_max = 131072   

Apply the changes:
 sysctl --system

Step 3: Restart kubelet
Restart kubelet so it can pick up the new CRI socket:
 sudo systemctl restart kubelet

Step 4: Verification
Confirm the CRI service and socket are active:
 sudo systemctl status cri-docker.socket cri-docker.service
 sudo ss -lx | grep cri-dockerd

Confirm the kernel values are applied:
 sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward
 sysctl net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables
 sysctl net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables

Optional: Confirm kubelet is healthy and the cluster is reachable:
 kubectl get nodes
 kubectl get pods -A

Important exam note:
- Use the local .deb package from the exam environment rather than downloading from the internet.
- Do not remove existing runtime configuration unless the task explicitly requires it.
- The CRI adapter socket is usually available at /var/run/cri-dockerd.sock.
